---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { EMAIL, EMAIL_HREF } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Charnwood Intimacy"
  description="How Charnwood Intimacy collects, uses and protects your personal information."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">
        Last updated 20 July 2026. This policy is adapted from Charnwood Counselling's existing
        privacy policy for this sibling site, and should be reviewed by Jo before the site goes
        live to confirm it reflects exactly what Charnwood Intimacy collects and uses.
      </p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Notice for Charnwood Intimacy ("we", "us" or "our") describes how and why we
        might access, collect, store, use and/or share ("process") your personal information when
        you use our services ("Services"), including when you visit our website at
        charnwoodintimacy.co.uk, or engage with us in other related ways, including bookings,
        enquiries or contact forms.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions or concerns? Reading this Privacy Notice will help you understand your privacy
        rights and choices. We are responsible for making decisions about how your personal
        information is processed. If you do not agree with our policies and practices, please do
        not use our Services. If you still have any questions or concerns, please contact us at{' '}
        <a href={EMAIL_HREF}>{EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What information do we collect?</h2>
      <p>
        We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us, for example through
        our contact and booking forms. This may include your name, email address, phone number
        and any message or additional information you choose to share with us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because of the nature of psychosexual therapy, some of the information you choose to
        share with us in a message, or in the course of therapy itself, may be considered
        sensitive personal information under data protection law, for example details relating to
        your health, sex life or sexual orientation. We only process this information with your
        consent, and it is treated with the same confidentiality that applies to all of Jo's
        clinical work.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also automatically collect some technical information when you visit our website, such
        as your approximate location, browser type, and how you interact with our pages. This
        helps us keep the site secure and understand how it's being used. See our{' '}
        <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for details of the specific cookies and
        technologies currently in use.
      </p>

      <h2>How do we use your information?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry or booking request</li>
        <li>To provide, manage and improve our therapy services</li>
        <li>To meet our legal, clinical and safeguarding obligations</li>
        <li>To keep a record of correspondence in line with good clinical practice</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What are our legal bases for processing?</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on your consent (for example, when you submit a contact form), on the performance
        of a contract (when arranging or providing therapy), and on our legitimate interests and
        legal obligations as a therapy practice, including safeguarding responsibilities.
      </p>

      <h2>Who do we share your information with?</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell or rent your personal information. We may share limited information with
        trusted third-party service providers who help us run this website and process enquiries,
        such as our contact form provider, and, where clinically or legally necessary, with
        relevant professional bodies, supervisors or authorities.
      </p>

      <h2>How long do we keep your information?</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal information only for as long as necessary for the purposes set out in
        this notice, or as required by our professional and legal obligations as a therapy
        practice.
      </p>

      <h2>How do we keep your information safe?</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your personal
        information. However, no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure,
        and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Do we collect information from minors?</h2>
      <p>
        Our Services are not directed at, and we do not knowingly collect information from,
        anyone under 18 years of age.
      </p>

      <h2>What are your privacy rights?</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law, you have rights including access to your personal
        information, correction of inaccurate data, erasure in certain circumstances, and the
        right to object to or restrict certain processing. To exercise any of these rights,
        please contact us using the details below. You also have the right to raise concerns with
        the{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions or concerns about this notice, please contact us at{' '}
        <a href={EMAIL_HREF}>{EMAIL}</a>, or by post at Charnwood Intimacy, Floor 2, The Old Arts
        College, 12 Frederick Street, Loughborough, LE11 3BJ.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 800px;
  }
  .prose p, .prose li {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .prose ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6em;
  }
  .updated {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--coral);
    padding-left: 16px;
  }
</style>
